From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:26:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Touch controls: per-button drag-to-aim and
 fire-on-release, fire mode toggle, hold RC on long press

Lets one thumb attack/shove and aim while the other moves, without a
third finger. Everything is off by default and set in the touch editor.

Per key/mouse button (tap a button in the editor):
- Drag to aim: while a finger is held on the button, dragging it also
  moves the cursor like PAD mode (8 pt dead zone; speed slider in the
  editor panel appears once any button uses it).
- Fire on release: holding does nothing (the button shows amber), so you
  can aim without spamming attacks; lifting the finger sends one press.
  Together with drag to aim: hold to aim, lift to fire once.

New "Fire mode toggle" button (Add menu): flips every Fire on release
button between release (REL) and plain hold (HOLD), shown on the button.

Global:
- Hold RC on long press: a 0.5 s press on a right-click button keeps it
  held after the finger lifts (gold ring + haptic). The next tap, ESC,
  hiding the controls, or connecting a controller lets go.

Untested on device: written against the public tree, not built in Xcode.

